{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Naphtali is a doe sent forth.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he blessed him with lightness, that the tribe of Naphtali would be swift as a doe, to run and announce good tidings and to inform them first — like that doe which announces by means of a written dispatch placed between its horns." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: נפתלי אילה שלוחה — this is the valley of Ginnosar, whose fruit ripens swiftly like a doe. <b>Who gives words of fairness</b> — that the tribe of Naphtali would honor the kings with their fruits and would present their words favorably, and the kings would be appeased toward them." "<b>Another interpretation.</b> נפתלי אילה שלוחה — this teaches that he sprang to Egypt like a doe, to bring the deed of the Cave (of Machpelah) to bury his father, and he did not have time to go, until Hushim son of Dan arose and killed Esau, because he was hindering the burial of Jacob; thus they interpreted in Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: נפתלי אילה שלוחה alludes to the righteous one, and he mentions in him אילה שלוחה because it is his, and it is Kenesset Yisrael, from the language of (Psalms 22) אילת השחר; and similarly שלוחה from the language of שליח; and this Naphtali gives אמרי שפר to the Holy One, blessed be He. And it is possible that Onkelos alluded to this. And thus our Rabbis of blessed memory said: one angel waits until the last prayer-congregation in Israel has prayed, and gathers all the prayers and makes them a crown for the head of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said (Proverbs 10): ברכות לראש צדיק; and it is known who is 'the head of the righteous one,' and this is clear."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:42.103767626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}